# The kernel's burn-down list against termlens: one `fixture/aspect` per line (tests/oracle.rs).
# Lower is better, and it only shrinks — a key that stops disagreeing must be removed.
# Seeded 2026-09-19 at 21, grouped in the order slice 3 burns them down
# (docs/design/terminal-kernel.md#next-slices).

# A DEFECT, not a missing report: Screen::line(n) returns vt100's LOGICAL line, so a soft-wrapped
# row reads as one long line while cell(r, c) addresses the grid — the two disagree about rows.
wrap/text

# Cursor position and visibility (vt100 tracks both; the kernel does not surface them).
clear_and_home/cursor
cursor_position/cursor
plain_text/cursor
wrap/cursor
cursor_hidden/cursor_visible

# Cursor shape (DECSCUSR) — vt100 0.15 does not track it; the kernel must.
cursor_shape_bar/cursor_shape
cursor_shape_block/cursor_shape

# The query responder (DA1 here): a capability probe waits out its timeout against the kernel.
query_device_attributes/text

# Recovered styles beyond bold.
sgr_attrs/cell(0,1).dim
sgr_attrs/cell(0,2).italic
sgr_attrs/cell(0,3).underline
sgr_attrs/cell(0,4).blink
sgr_attrs/cell(0,5).reverse
sgr_attrs/cell(0,6).conceal
sgr_attrs/cell(0,7).strikethrough

# Out-of-band state and input modes.
title/title
alternate_screen/alternate_screen
input_modes/application_cursor
input_modes/bracketed_paste
input_modes/mouse_reporting
